sapphire: a UBWC flip takes the metadata of the frame it shows

0398 programmed SSPP_SRC2_ADDR and YSTRIDE1 from fQ[fQCount - 1], the newest frame still queued. The frame being shown
has already left the queue when planeScaled() runs (queueStep() and queueDrain() take it out first), so the plane
fetched one surface's colour data with another surface's metadata, or, with the queue empty, kept the metadata of an
earlier frame. Read on the phone: SRC0_ADDR e5007000 with SRC2_ADDR e5a00000 (pool slots are 0x500000 apart), and
UBWC_ERROR_STATUS set on 9 of 10 flips, the screen covered in green blocks. planeScaled() now receives the frame and
uses its own metaPa, metaStride and ubwc flag.

A linear frame after UBWC ones restores the plane's linear registers (SRC2_ADDR, YSTRIDE1, SRC_FORMAT, UNPACK,
OP_MODE, UBWC_STATIC_CTRL, FETCH_CONFIG, as found at the first UBWC flip, and SRC_XY): 0398 left them in UBWC mode.

